{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c525","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":237,"recorded_at":1780531400000469,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1eb-5588-7f12-8c78-b19f7ffa14e9"},"task_id":"01a0b1eb-5588-7f12-8c78-b19f7ffa14e9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1eb-5588-7f12-8c78-b19f7ffa14e9","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(1039 line(s) above)\n1040|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1041|\n1042|Terminal Backend Protocol 1.0.0 has a closed request envelope containing\n1043|exactly <code>protocol</code> with literal\n1044|<code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code>,\n1045|<code>protocol_version</code> with exact value <code>1.0.0</code>,\n1046|<code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>operation</code>, and <code>body</code>.\n1047|Its response repeats those three identity members exactly and contains\n1048|<code>ok:true,result:&lt;operation-success-body&gt;</code> or\n1049|<code>ok:false,error:StructuredError1.3</code>, never both result and error.\n1050|Operation is one of the ten names in Section 4.C and the exact bodies are its\n1051|typed matrix. Unknown members, operations, or body variants are protocol\n1052|errors. This is an AX-controlled local adapter wire, not a stable public SDK.\n1053|\n1054|AX allocates <code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>. Terminal Instance Binding\n1055|1.0.0 is the following closed immutable host-local object; no other member is\n1056|permitted:\n1057|\n1058|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1059|| --- | --- |\n1060|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding</code> |\n1061|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1062|| <code>binding_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule above |\n1063|| <code>session_id</code> | Logical Session UUIDv7 |\n1064|| <code>host_id</code> | AX Host UUIDv7 |\n1065|| <code>host_incarnation_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated once for the current host-agent process incarnation |\n1066|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-allocated UUIDv7 |\n1067|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1068|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to admitted Manifest and Probe |\n1069|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe |\n1070|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\n1071|| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\n1072|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp |\n1073|| <code>supersedes_binding_id</code> | digest|null; null only for the first binding of this Session on this host incarnation |\n1074|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1075|\n1076|Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or\n1077|mutable endpoint. Binding is host/incarnation-local and does not alter Logical\n1078|Session identity. Boundary conformance cases MUST reject generation lengths 0\n1079|and 257 and accept length 256 in the Binding, Provider Protocol 3 descriptor,\n1080|operation bodies, and CLI Result 4 summary.\n1081|\n1082|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1083|\n1084|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1085|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1086|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1087|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1088|\n1089|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1090|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1091|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1092|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1093|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1094|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1095|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1096|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1097|\n1098|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1099|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1100|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1101|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1102|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1103|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1104|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1105|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1106|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1107|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1108|\n1109|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1110|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1111|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1112|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1113|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1114|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1115|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1116|\n1117|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1118|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1119|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1120|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1121|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1122|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1123|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1124|\n1125|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1126|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1127|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1128|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1129|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1130|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1131|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1132|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1133|\n1134|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1135|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1136|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1137|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1138|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1139|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1140|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1141|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1142|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1143|\n1144|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1145|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1146|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1147|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1148|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1149|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1150|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1151|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1152|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1153|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1154|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1155|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1156|\n1157|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1158|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1159|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1160|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1161|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1162|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1163|persisted or replicated.\n1164|\n1165|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1166|| --- | --- | --- |\n1167|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1168|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1169|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1170|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1171|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1172|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1173|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1174|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1175|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1176|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1177|\n1178|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1179|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1180|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1181|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1182|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n1183|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n1184|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n1185|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n1186|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n1187|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n1188|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n1189|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n1190|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n1191|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n1192|\n1193|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n1194|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n1195|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n1196|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n1197|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n1198|transition and no side effect.\n1199|\n1200|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n1201|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1202|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1203|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1204|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1205|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1206|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1207|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1208|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1209|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1210|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1211|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1212|\n1213|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n1214|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n1215|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n1216|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n1217|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n1218|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n1219|\n1220|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1221|\n1222|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n1223|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n1224|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n1225|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n1226|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n1227|\n1228|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1229|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n1230|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n1231|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n1232|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n1233|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n1234|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n1235|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n1236|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n1237|\n1238|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n1239|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1240|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1241|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1242|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1243|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1244|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1245|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1246|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1247|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1248|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1249|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1250|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1251|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1252|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1253|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1254|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n1255|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1256|\n1257|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n1258|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n1259|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n1260|member is permitted:\n1261|\n1262|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1263|| --- | --- |\n1264|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n1265|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1266|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n1267|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1268|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n1269|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n1270|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n1271|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n1272|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1273|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1274|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1275|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1276|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1277|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1278|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1279|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1280|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1281|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1282|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1283|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1284|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1285|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1286|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1287|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1288|\n1289|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1290|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1291|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1292|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1293|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1294|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1295|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1296|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1297|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1298|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1299|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1300|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1301|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1302|change and before activation.\n1303|\n1304|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1305|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1306|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1307|activation when policy allows.\n1308|\n1309|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n1310|\n1311|| Classification | Members and rule |\n1312|| --- | --- |\n1313|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n1314|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n1315|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n1316|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n1317|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n1318|\n1319|Presentation transport is exactly <code>local_only</code>,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c527","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":238,"recorded_at":1780531400000471,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1eb-5588-7f12-8c78-b19f7ffa14e9"},"task_id":"01a0b1eb-5588-7f12-8c78-b19f7ffa14e9","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b1eb-5588-7f12-8c78-b19f7ffa14e9"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c529","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":239,"recorded_at":1780531400000473,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1eb5089707b837d19aec31043ed","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(1039 line(s) above)\n1040|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1041|\n1042|Terminal Backend Protocol 1.0.0 has a closed request envelope containing\n1043|exactly <code>protocol</code> with literal\n1044|<code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code>,\n1045|<code>protocol_version</code> with exact value <code>1.0.0</code>,\n1046|<code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>operation</code>, and <code>body</code>.\n1047|Its response repeats those three identity members exactly and contains\n1048|<code>ok:true,result:&lt;operation-success-body&gt;</code> or\n1049|<code>ok:false,error:StructuredError1.3</code>, never both result and error.\n1050|Operation is one of the ten names in Section 4.C and the exact bodies are its\n1051|typed matrix. Unknown members, operations, or body variants are protocol\n1052|errors. This is an AX-controlled local adapter wire, not a stable public SDK.\n1053|\n1054|AX allocates <code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>. Terminal Instance Binding\n1055|1.0.0 is the following closed immutable host-local object; no other member is\n1056|permitted:\n1057|\n1058|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1059|| --- | --- |\n1060|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding</code> |\n1061|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1062|| <code>binding_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule above |\n1063|| <code>session_id</code> | Logical Session UUIDv7 |\n1064|| <code>host_id</code> | AX Host UUIDv7 |\n1065|| <code>host_incarnation_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated once for the current host-agent process incarnation |\n1066|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-allocated UUIDv7 |\n1067|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1068|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to admitted Manifest and Probe |\n1069|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe |\n1070|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\n1071|| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\n1072|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp |\n1073|| <code>supersedes_binding_id</code> | digest|null; null only for the first binding of this Session on this host incarnation |\n1074|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1075|\n1076|Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or\n1077|mutable endpoint. Binding is host/incarnation-local and does not alter Logical\n1078|Session identity. Boundary conformance cases MUST reject generation lengths 0\n1079|and 257 and accept length 256 in the Binding, Provider Protocol 3 descriptor,\n1080|operation bodies, and CLI Result 4 summary.\n1081|\n1082|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1083|\n1084|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1085|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1086|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1087|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1088|\n1089|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1090|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1091|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1092|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1093|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1094|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1095|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1096|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1097|\n1098|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1099|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1100|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1101|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1102|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1103|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1104|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1105|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1106|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1107|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1108|\n1109|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1110|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1111|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1112|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1113|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1114|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1115|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1116|\n1117|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1118|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1119|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1120|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1121|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1122|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1123|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1124|\n1125|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1126|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1127|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1128|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1129|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1130|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1131|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1132|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1133|\n1134|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1135|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1136|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1137|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1138|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1139|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1140|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1141|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1142|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1143|\n1144|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1145|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1146|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1147|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1148|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1149|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1150|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1151|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1152|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1153|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1154|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1155|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1156|\n1157|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1158|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1159|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1160|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1161|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1162|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1163|persisted or replicated.\n1164|\n1165|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1166|| --- | --- | --- |\n1167|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1168|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1169|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1170|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1171|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1172|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1173|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1174|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1175|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1176|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1177|\n1178|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1179|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1180|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1181|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1182|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n1183|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n1184|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n1185|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n1186|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n1187|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n1188|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n1189|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n1190|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n1191|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n1192|\n1193|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n1194|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n1195|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n1196|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n1197|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n1198|transition and no side effect.\n1199|\n1200|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n1201|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1202|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1203|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1204|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1205|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1206|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1207|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1208|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1209|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1210|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1211|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1212|\n1213|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n1214|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n1215|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n1216|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n1217|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n1218|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n1219|\n1220|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1221|\n1222|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n1223|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n1224|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n1225|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n1226|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n1227|\n1228|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1229|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n1230|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n1231|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n1232|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n1233|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n1234|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n1235|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n1236|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n1237|\n1238|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n1239|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1240|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1241|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1242|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1243|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1244|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1245|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1246|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1247|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1248|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1249|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1250|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1251|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1252|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1253|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1254|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n1255|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1256|\n1257|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n1258|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n1259|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n1260|member is permitted:\n1261|\n1262|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1263|| --- | --- |\n1264|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n1265|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1266|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n1267|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1268|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n1269|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n1270|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n1271|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n1272|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1273|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1274|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1275|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1276|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1277|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1278|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1279|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1280|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1281|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1282|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1283|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1284|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1285|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1286|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1287|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1288|\n1289|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1290|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1291|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1292|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1293|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1294|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1295|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1296|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1297|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1298|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1299|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1300|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1301|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1302|change and before activation.\n1303|\n1304|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1305|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1306|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1307|activation when policy allows.\n1308|\n1309|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n1310|\n1311|| Classification | Members and rule |\n1312|| --- | --- |\n1313|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n1314|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n1315|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n1316|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n1317|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n1318|\n1319|Presentation transport is exactly <code>local_only</code>,\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
