{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c58d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":289,"recorded_at":1780531400000573,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1eb-7646-7252-88c7-3c763ed9e999"},"task_id":"01a0b1eb-7646-7252-88c7-3c763ed9e999","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1eb-7646-7252-88c7-3c763ed9e999","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(1955 line(s) above)\n1956|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1957|\n1958|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1959|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1960|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1961|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1962|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1963|\n1964|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1965|| --- | --- |\n1966|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1967|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1968|\n1969|The binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\n1970|Instance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\n1971|replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\n1972|Manifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\n1973|backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\n1974|reference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\n1975|terminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\n1976|\n1977|<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\n1978|authorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\n1979|that owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\n1980|admitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\n1981|does not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\n1982|Attach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\n1983|Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\n1984|as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\n1985|version replacement.\n1986|\n1987|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n1988|\n1989|The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\n1990|<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\n1991|\n1992|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1993|| --- | --- | --- |\n1994|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\n1995|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1996|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\n1997|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1998|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Cryptographically random unique fencing token |\n1999|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\n2000|| <code>epoch</code> | uint53 | Starts at 1; never decreases |\n2001|| <code>holder_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Proposed owner |\n2002|| <code>predecessor_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 or null | Null only at epoch 1 |\n2003|| <code>reason</code> | enum | <code>create</code>, <code>graceful_takeover</code>, <code>force_takeover</code>, <code>recovery</code> |\n2004|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for epoch-1 <code>create</code>; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base |\n2005|| <code>issued_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Initiator |\n2006|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |\n2007|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2008|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2009|\n2010|The object is closed; every row is required, including nullable fields.\n2011|Normative example:\n2012|\n2013|~~~json\n2014|{\n2015|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:lease\",\n2016|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2017|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:8ead987abed8c7c05175b447c9a0e2b3a521f12e5a989acb8abe132576852d63\",\n2018|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2019|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2020|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n2021|  \"epoch\": 4,\n2022|  \"holder_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n2023|  \"predecessor_lease_id\": \"bbbbbbbb-cccc-4ddd-8eee-ffffffffffff\",\n2024|  \"reason\": \"graceful_takeover\",\n2025|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2026|  \"issued_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n2027|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n2028|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:00.000Z\",\n2029|  \"extensions\": {}\n2030|}\n2031|~~~\n2032|\n2033|The winning lease is selected by the greatest tuple\n2034|<code>(epoch, lease_id)</code>, where <code>lease_id</code> uses bytewise UUID\n2035|order. Lease UUIDs are random UUIDv4 values, so wall-clock skew cannot bias the\n2036|tie-break. A valid epoch greater than 1 MUST name a known predecessor for the\n2037|same session, MUST equal that predecessor's epoch plus one, and MUST reference\n2038|a validated checkpoint for that session and predecessor lease. An epoch-1\n2039|<code>create</code> lease MUST have a null predecessor and MAY have a null\n2040|checkpoint before the first provider boundary exists. Every new takeover lease\n2041|MUST use <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code> from the initiator's current union.\n2042|\n2043|The tuple rule handles concurrent force takeovers under partition without\n2044|clock ordering. Both processes can temporarily continue in isolated partitions,\n2045|which is why force takeover warns about split brain. After union, exactly one\n2046|lease wins. Events under the losing same-epoch lease and all lower epochs MUST\n2047|be preserved in a divergent branch and MUST NOT affect authoritative state.\n2048|\n2049|An owner process MUST revalidate its fencing token before:\n2050|\n2051|- accepting operator input after attach;\n2052|- starting a provider turn;\n2053|- publishing a checkpoint;\n2054|- pushing records or workspace changes; and\n2055|- resuming after any transport or sleep interruption longer than the configured\n2056|  lease refresh interval.\n2057|\n2058|There is no time-expiring ownership lease in v0.5.0. Liveness is not authority.\n2059|A host being offline does not make a replica owner; only a takeover or fork\n2060|does.\n2061|\n2062|### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n2063|\n2064|The Checkpoint Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:checkpoint</code> version\n2065|<code>1.0.0</code>. Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2066|\n2067|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2068|| --- | --- | --- |\n2069|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Checkpoint schema identifier |\n2070|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2071|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n2072|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n2073|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing Session Record |\n2074|| <code>lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero and equal to the referenced winning lease |\n2075|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Equal to that lease's fencing token |\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
