{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c595","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":293,"recorded_at":1780531400000581,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1eb6dd875d48a4f1d77c954afbf","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(1955 line(s) above)\n1956|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1957|\n1958|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1959|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1960|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1961|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1962|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1963|\n1964|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1965|| --- | --- |\n1966|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1967|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1968|\n1969|The binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\n1970|Instance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\n1971|replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\n1972|Manifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\n1973|backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\n1974|reference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\n1975|terminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\n1976|\n1977|<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\n1978|authorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\n1979|that owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\n1980|admitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\n1981|does not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\n1982|Attach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\n1983|Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\n1984|as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\n1985|version replacement.\n1986|\n1987|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n1988|\n1989|The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\n1990|<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\n1991|\n1992|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1993|| --- | --- | --- |\n1994|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\n1995|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1996|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\n1997|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n1998|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Cryptographically random unique fencing token |\n1999|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\n2000|| <code>epoch</code> | uint53 | Starts at 1; never decreases |\n2001|| <code>holder_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Proposed owner |\n2002|| <code>predecessor_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 or null | Null only at epoch 1 |\n2003|| <code>reason</code> | enum | <code>create</code>, <code>graceful_takeover</code>, <code>force_takeover</code>, <code>recovery</code> |\n2004|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for epoch-1 <code>create</code>; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base |\n2005|| <code>issued_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Initiator |\n2006|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |\n2007|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2008|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2009|\n2010|The object is closed; every row is required, including nullable fields.\n2011|Normative example:\n2012|\n2013|~~~json\n2014|{\n2015|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:lease\",\n2016|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2017|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:8ead987abed8c7c05175b447c9a0e2b3a521f12e5a989acb8abe132576852d63\",\n2018|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2019|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2020|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n2021|  \"epoch\": 4,\n2022|  \"holder_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n2023|  \"predecessor_lease_id\": \"bbbbbbbb-cccc-4ddd-8eee-ffffffffffff\",\n2024|  \"reason\": \"graceful_takeover\",\n2025|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2026|  \"issued_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n2027|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-7d40-7e55-8e6f-1234567890ab\",\n2028|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:00.000Z\",\n2029|  \"extensions\": {}\n2030|}\n2031|~~~\n2032|\n2033|The winning lease is selected by the greatest tuple\n2034|<code>(epoch, lease_id)</code>, where <code>lease_id</code> uses bytewise UUID\n2035|order. Lease UUIDs are random UUIDv4 values, so wall-clock skew cannot bias the\n2036|tie-break. A valid epoch greater than 1 MUST name a known predecessor for the\n2037|same session, MUST equal that predecessor's epoch plus one, and MUST reference\n2038|a validated checkpoint for that session and predecessor lease. An epoch-1\n2039|<code>create</code> lease MUST have a null predecessor and MAY have a null\n2040|checkpoint before the first provider boundary exists. Every new takeover lease\n2041|MUST use <code>max_observed_epoch + 1</code> from the initiator's current union.\n2042|\n2043|The tuple rule handles concurrent force takeovers under partition without\n2044|clock ordering. Both processes can temporarily continue in isolated partitions,\n2045|which is why force takeover warns about split brain. After union, exactly one\n2046|lease wins. Events under the losing same-epoch lease and all lower epochs MUST\n2047|be preserved in a divergent branch and MUST NOT affect authoritative state.\n2048|\n2049|An owner process MUST revalidate its fencing token before:\n2050|\n2051|- accepting operator input after attach;\n2052|- starting a provider turn;\n2053|- publishing a checkpoint;\n2054|- pushing records or workspace changes; and\n2055|- resuming after any transport or sleep interruption longer than the configured\n2056|  lease refresh interval.\n2057|\n2058|There is no time-expiring ownership lease in v0.5.0. Liveness is not authority.\n2059|A host being offline does not make a replica owner; only a takeover or fork\n2060|does.\n2061|\n2062|### 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n2063|\n2064|The Checkpoint Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:checkpoint</code> version\n2065|<code>1.0.0</code>. Its top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2066|\n2067|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2068|| --- | --- | --- |\n2069|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Checkpoint schema identifier |\n2070|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2071|| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n2072|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n2073|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing Session Record |\n2074|| <code>lease_epoch</code> | uint53 | Greater than zero and equal to the referenced winning lease |\n2075|| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Equal to that lease's fencing token |\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c597","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":294,"recorded_at":1780531400000583,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1eb718775cfa0c2870aa570627d","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(3702 line(s) above)\n3703|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3704|\n3705|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3706|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3707|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3708|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3709|\n3710|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3711|| --- | --- |\n3712|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3713|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3714|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3715|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3716|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3717|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3718|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3719|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3720|\n3721|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3722|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3723|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3724|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3725|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3726|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3727|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3728|\n3729|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3730|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3731|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3732|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3733|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3734|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3735|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3736|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3737|\n3738|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3739|\n3740|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3741|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3742|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3743|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3744|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3745|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3746|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3747|\n3748|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3749|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3750|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3751|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3752|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3753|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3754|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3755|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3756|\n3757|The closed operation registry is:\n3758|\n3759|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3760|| --- | --- |\n3761|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3762|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3763|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3764|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3765|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3766|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3767|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3768|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3769|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3770|\n3771|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3772|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3773|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3774|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3775|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3776|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3777|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3778|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3779|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3780|every candidate object.\n3781|\n3782|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
