{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":317,"recorded_at":1780531400000629,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1eb-85d0-7f01-b677-88910d11024c"},"task_id":"01a0b1eb-85d0-7f01-b677-88910d11024c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1eb-85d0-7f01-b677-88910d11024c","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(9171 line(s) above)\n9172|## 13. End-to-end lifecycle flows\n9173|\n9174|Every mutating flow has a UUIDv7 <code>operation_id</code>. A retry with the\n9175|same operation ID and inputs MUST be idempotent. A retry with different inputs\n9176|MUST fail with <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n9177|\n9178|### 13.1 Direct-session launch\n9179|\n9180|Preconditions:\n9181|\n9182|- configuration and local host identity are valid;\n9183|- the session name is unused across the reachable mesh;\n9184|- the provider plugin is trusted and <code>probe</code> succeeds;\n9185|- requested profile mapping is available;\n9186|- destination workspace is validated or captured as a new managed workspace;\n9187|- the terminal backend is available; and\n9188|- no task-board fields are supplied.\n9189|\n9190|Transitions:\n9191|\n9192|1. Allocate session, caller-stable bootstrap-operation,\n9193|   first-checkpoint-operation, and initial lease IDs. If the workspace has a\n9194|   valid current managed-replica marker, reuse its unique Workspace Group\n9195|   Record after exact topology validation; otherwise allocate new workspace-\n9196|   group/workspace IDs and one new group record. Epoch is 1 and the local host\n9197|   is the holder.\n9198|2. Persist any new Workspace Group Record, then the Session Record referencing\n9199|   that group, the initial Lease Record, and <code>session.created</code> carrying\n9200|   both operation IDs before creating a process. Joining\n9201|   an existing group publishes no group update; derived membership changes by\n9202|   union of the new Session Record.\n9203|3. Create the durable terminal entry <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code> with the\n9204|   bootstrap operation ID.\n9205|4. Call provider <code>launch</code> and validate its argv/env-name plan.\n9206|5. Start the provider through the terminal backend with the epoch-1 fencing\n9207|   token and persisted profile. Persist <code>provider.launched</code> with\n9208|   <code>execution_profile</code> equal to the Session Record and\n9209|   <code>profile_source_event_id = null</code>.\n9210|6. Call <code>identify-session</code>; persist the Provider Identity Record and\n9211|   <code>provider.identified</code> event.\n9212|7. When the first safe boundary is observed, create the workspace-group root\n9213|   manifest. If <code>portable_store</code> is enabled, call provider\n9214|   <code>native-store-plan phase=capture</code> and <code>capture</code> with the\n9215|   first-checkpoint operation ID into an\n9216|   isolated Object Sink; otherwise create a zero-entry provider manifest that\n9217|   references the exact Provider Identity Record. Validate both, then publish\n9218|   the direct-path checkpoint with a non-null provider manifest.\n9219|8. Publish immutable objects for replica sync and report <code>running</code>\n9220|   or <code>idle</code>.\n9221|\n9222|When the launch carries a caller-supplied plan (Section 14.1\n9223|<code>--launch-plan</code>), one step precedes step 2 for both document forms.\n9224|<code>ax</code> calls provider <code>launch</code> with the candidate Session\n9225|Record in planning role — provider <code>launch</code> is already a\n9226|plan-returning operation that creates no process (Section 7.5) — takes the\n9227|returned <code>SpawnPlan.argv</code> as the resolved final argv (the plugin's\n9228|base argv followed by the document's <code>argv_suffix</code>; for the\n9229|<code>argv</code> form, the plugin's verbatim translation after its Section\n9230|7.7 profile-flag check), validates it under the Section 5.1 argv limits\n9231|(1..128 elements, each 1–4,096 bytes, at most 65,536 encoded bytes), and only\n9232|then persists the record with <code>launch_plan.argv</code> equal to that\n9233|final argv, so the immutable record answers \"what launched\" without\n9234|re-deriving anything. Every refusal of this step — shape, limit, exclusivity,\n9235|unknown member, extension collision or bound, secret, profile flag, or\n9236|missing capability — fires before any Session Record, lease, terminal entry,\n9237|or process exists. A plugin declaring <code>caller_launch_plan</code> MUST\n9238|answer the planning call deterministically, and step 4's <code>launch</code>\n9239|against the persisted record MUST return an argv equal to the recorded one;\n9240|a mismatch is <code>provider_protocol_error</code> and no process is created.\n9241|\n9242|The record carries the caller document under the <code>ax</code>-generic\n9243|top-level <code>extensions</code> key <code>ax.launch-plan-request</code>, a\n9244|closed object\n9245|<code>{form: \"argv\" | \"argv_suffix\", base_argv_length: uint53, request_digest: digest}</code>.\n9246|The <code>ax</code> label mirrors the <code>urn:ax</code> authority of every\n9247|schema identifier in Section 1.5. The document itself is not stored: the\n9248|Section 1.6 extension bound is 65,536 canonical bytes, and a document may\n9249|carry 65,536 bytes of argv plus 65,536 bytes of stdin. For the same reason the\n9250|value carries no copy of the suffix: <code>launch_plan.argv</code> already\n9251|holds it, and the suffix is defined as\n9252|<code>launch_plan.argv[base_argv_length:]</code> (for the <code>argv</code>\n9253|form <code>base_argv_length</code> is 0 and the suffix is the whole argv).\n9254|That definition is what resume replays (Section 7.5) and what lets a reader\n9255|split the recorded final argv into its two owners; the value is a few dozen\n9256|bytes regardless of the plan's size. <code>request_digest</code> is the\n9257|Section 1.6 SHA-256 digest of the JCS canonical bytes of the caller document\n9258|and lets an operator prove which document produced the record; it is a record,\n9259|not a signature. The caller's own <code>extensions</code> — for a\n9260|Curator-composed document the four <code>works.relux.curator.*</code> keys of\n9261|Section 5.1 are among them; <code>ax</code> is generic and knows no such class\n9262|— together with this key MUST fit the Section 1.6 extensions bound (at most 64\n9263|keys, canonical object at most 65,536 bytes) as they will be persisted; a\n9264|document that would not is refused in the planning step with\n9265|<code>launch_plan_invalid</code>, <code>field: \"extensions\"</code>, so no\n9266|document that passes validation can yield a record <code>ax</code> cannot\n9267|persist.\n9268|\n9269|The caller-plan path has these required conformance cases; Appendix D binds\n9270|them to <code>fixtures/launch_plan_request_conformance.json</code>:\n9271|\n9272|| Fixture | Input | Required result |\n9273|| --- | --- | --- |\n9274|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-SUFFIX-POS</code> | <code>argv_suffix</code> document under <code>--profile standard</code> against a <code>caller_launch_plan</code> plugin | Record persisted with <code>launch_plan.argv</code> equal to the plugin's base argv followed by the suffix and <code>ax.launch-plan-request</code> <code>{form: \"argv_suffix\", base_argv_length: &lt;base length&gt;, request_digest}</code>; step 4 returns the recorded argv |\n9275|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-ARGV-POS</code> | <code>argv</code> document whose element 0 is the plugin-resolved executable, <code>--profile standard</code> | Plugin appends nothing; <code>base_argv_length</code> is 0; recorded argv equals the document's |\n9276|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-PROFILE-FLAG-NEG</code> | <code>argv</code> or <code>argv_suffix</code> carries the provider's own Section 7.7 <code>yolo</code> flag, long form or documented alias, under <code>--profile standard</code> | <code>launch_plan_invalid</code>, <code>reason: \"profile_flag\"</code>, <code>details.argv_index</code> the element's index in the final argv; no Session Record or process |\n9277|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-SECRET-NEG</code> | An <code>env_literals</code> value or <code>stdin</code> payload the Section 5.1 secret rule or Section 16.2 exclusions classify | <code>secret_policy_violation</code> (exit 16), <code>details.field</code> naming the member; no Session Record |\n9278|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-EXTENSIONS-NEG</code> | Caller <code>extensions</code> that with <code>ax.launch-plan-request</code> and the Curator keys exceed the Section 1.6 bound | <code>launch_plan_invalid</code>, <code>field: \"extensions\"</code>; no Session Record |\n9279|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-CAPABILITY-NEG</code> | Any document against a plugin whose manifest does not declare <code>caller_launch_plan</code> | <code>capability_unavailable</code>, <code>details.capability: \"caller_launch_plan\"</code>, before the plugin is invoked |\n9280|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-DETERMINISM-NEG</code> | Plugin returns at step 4 an argv different from its planning-role answer | <code>provider_protocol_error</code>; no process |\n9281|\n9282|Each negative case is proven by a test that fails when the gate admits the\n9283|input, driven through the real <code>ax start --launch-plan</code> entry point;\n9284|a delete-only mutant is insufficient (Appendix D.1), and the profile-flag case\n9285|MUST also survive a narrowing mutant that drops one documented alias.\n9286|\n9287|The first-checkpoint operation ID keys the capture/export and checkpoint-\n9288|publication transaction even when a backend-only provider emits a zero-entry\n9289|manifest. An identical retry reuses the same immutable objects and event;\n9290|changing either operation ID after <code>session.created</code> is\n9291|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":318,"recorded_at":1780531400000631,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1eb-85d0-7f01-b677-88910d11024c"},"task_id":"01a0b1eb-85d0-7f01-b677-88910d11024c","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b1eb-85d0-7f01-b677-88910d11024c"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":319,"recorded_at":1780531400000633,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1eb7f8e7761acd4cb1d3617ed99","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(9171 line(s) above)\n9172|## 13. End-to-end lifecycle flows\n9173|\n9174|Every mutating flow has a UUIDv7 <code>operation_id</code>. A retry with the\n9175|same operation ID and inputs MUST be idempotent. A retry with different inputs\n9176|MUST fail with <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n9177|\n9178|### 13.1 Direct-session launch\n9179|\n9180|Preconditions:\n9181|\n9182|- configuration and local host identity are valid;\n9183|- the session name is unused across the reachable mesh;\n9184|- the provider plugin is trusted and <code>probe</code> succeeds;\n9185|- requested profile mapping is available;\n9186|- destination workspace is validated or captured as a new managed workspace;\n9187|- the terminal backend is available; and\n9188|- no task-board fields are supplied.\n9189|\n9190|Transitions:\n9191|\n9192|1. Allocate session, caller-stable bootstrap-operation,\n9193|   first-checkpoint-operation, and initial lease IDs. If the workspace has a\n9194|   valid current managed-replica marker, reuse its unique Workspace Group\n9195|   Record after exact topology validation; otherwise allocate new workspace-\n9196|   group/workspace IDs and one new group record. Epoch is 1 and the local host\n9197|   is the holder.\n9198|2. Persist any new Workspace Group Record, then the Session Record referencing\n9199|   that group, the initial Lease Record, and <code>session.created</code> carrying\n9200|   both operation IDs before creating a process. Joining\n9201|   an existing group publishes no group update; derived membership changes by\n9202|   union of the new Session Record.\n9203|3. Create the durable terminal entry <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code> with the\n9204|   bootstrap operation ID.\n9205|4. Call provider <code>launch</code> and validate its argv/env-name plan.\n9206|5. Start the provider through the terminal backend with the epoch-1 fencing\n9207|   token and persisted profile. Persist <code>provider.launched</code> with\n9208|   <code>execution_profile</code> equal to the Session Record and\n9209|   <code>profile_source_event_id = null</code>.\n9210|6. Call <code>identify-session</code>; persist the Provider Identity Record and\n9211|   <code>provider.identified</code> event.\n9212|7. When the first safe boundary is observed, create the workspace-group root\n9213|   manifest. If <code>portable_store</code> is enabled, call provider\n9214|   <code>native-store-plan phase=capture</code> and <code>capture</code> with the\n9215|   first-checkpoint operation ID into an\n9216|   isolated Object Sink; otherwise create a zero-entry provider manifest that\n9217|   references the exact Provider Identity Record. Validate both, then publish\n9218|   the direct-path checkpoint with a non-null provider manifest.\n9219|8. Publish immutable objects for replica sync and report <code>running</code>\n9220|   or <code>idle</code>.\n9221|\n9222|When the launch carries a caller-supplied plan (Section 14.1\n9223|<code>--launch-plan</code>), one step precedes step 2 for both document forms.\n9224|<code>ax</code> calls provider <code>launch</code> with the candidate Session\n9225|Record in planning role — provider <code>launch</code> is already a\n9226|plan-returning operation that creates no process (Section 7.5) — takes the\n9227|returned <code>SpawnPlan.argv</code> as the resolved final argv (the plugin's\n9228|base argv followed by the document's <code>argv_suffix</code>; for the\n9229|<code>argv</code> form, the plugin's verbatim translation after its Section\n9230|7.7 profile-flag check), validates it under the Section 5.1 argv limits\n9231|(1..128 elements, each 1–4,096 bytes, at most 65,536 encoded bytes), and only\n9232|then persists the record with <code>launch_plan.argv</code> equal to that\n9233|final argv, so the immutable record answers \"what launched\" without\n9234|re-deriving anything. Every refusal of this step — shape, limit, exclusivity,\n9235|unknown member, extension collision or bound, secret, profile flag, or\n9236|missing capability — fires before any Session Record, lease, terminal entry,\n9237|or process exists. A plugin declaring <code>caller_launch_plan</code> MUST\n9238|answer the planning call deterministically, and step 4's <code>launch</code>\n9239|against the persisted record MUST return an argv equal to the recorded one;\n9240|a mismatch is <code>provider_protocol_error</code> and no process is created.\n9241|\n9242|The record carries the caller document under the <code>ax</code>-generic\n9243|top-level <code>extensions</code> key <code>ax.launch-plan-request</code>, a\n9244|closed object\n9245|<code>{form: \"argv\" | \"argv_suffix\", base_argv_length: uint53, request_digest: digest}</code>.\n9246|The <code>ax</code> label mirrors the <code>urn:ax</code> authority of every\n9247|schema identifier in Section 1.5. The document itself is not stored: the\n9248|Section 1.6 extension bound is 65,536 canonical bytes, and a document may\n9249|carry 65,536 bytes of argv plus 65,536 bytes of stdin. For the same reason the\n9250|value carries no copy of the suffix: <code>launch_plan.argv</code> already\n9251|holds it, and the suffix is defined as\n9252|<code>launch_plan.argv[base_argv_length:]</code> (for the <code>argv</code>\n9253|form <code>base_argv_length</code> is 0 and the suffix is the whole argv).\n9254|That definition is what resume replays (Section 7.5) and what lets a reader\n9255|split the recorded final argv into its two owners; the value is a few dozen\n9256|bytes regardless of the plan's size. <code>request_digest</code> is the\n9257|Section 1.6 SHA-256 digest of the JCS canonical bytes of the caller document\n9258|and lets an operator prove which document produced the record; it is a record,\n9259|not a signature. The caller's own <code>extensions</code> — for a\n9260|Curator-composed document the four <code>works.relux.curator.*</code> keys of\n9261|Section 5.1 are among them; <code>ax</code> is generic and knows no such class\n9262|— together with this key MUST fit the Section 1.6 extensions bound (at most 64\n9263|keys, canonical object at most 65,536 bytes) as they will be persisted; a\n9264|document that would not is refused in the planning step with\n9265|<code>launch_plan_invalid</code>, <code>field: \"extensions\"</code>, so no\n9266|document that passes validation can yield a record <code>ax</code> cannot\n9267|persist.\n9268|\n9269|The caller-plan path has these required conformance cases; Appendix D binds\n9270|them to <code>fixtures/launch_plan_request_conformance.json</code>:\n9271|\n9272|| Fixture | Input | Required result |\n9273|| --- | --- | --- |\n9274|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-SUFFIX-POS</code> | <code>argv_suffix</code> document under <code>--profile standard</code> against a <code>caller_launch_plan</code> plugin | Record persisted with <code>launch_plan.argv</code> equal to the plugin's base argv followed by the suffix and <code>ax.launch-plan-request</code> <code>{form: \"argv_suffix\", base_argv_length: &lt;base length&gt;, request_digest}</code>; step 4 returns the recorded argv |\n9275|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-ARGV-POS</code> | <code>argv</code> document whose element 0 is the plugin-resolved executable, <code>--profile standard</code> | Plugin appends nothing; <code>base_argv_length</code> is 0; recorded argv equals the document's |\n9276|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-PROFILE-FLAG-NEG</code> | <code>argv</code> or <code>argv_suffix</code> carries the provider's own Section 7.7 <code>yolo</code> flag, long form or documented alias, under <code>--profile standard</code> | <code>launch_plan_invalid</code>, <code>reason: \"profile_flag\"</code>, <code>details.argv_index</code> the element's index in the final argv; no Session Record or process |\n9277|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-SECRET-NEG</code> | An <code>env_literals</code> value or <code>stdin</code> payload the Section 5.1 secret rule or Section 16.2 exclusions classify | <code>secret_policy_violation</code> (exit 16), <code>details.field</code> naming the member; no Session Record |\n9278|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-EXTENSIONS-NEG</code> | Caller <code>extensions</code> that with <code>ax.launch-plan-request</code> and the Curator keys exceed the Section 1.6 bound | <code>launch_plan_invalid</code>, <code>field: \"extensions\"</code>; no Session Record |\n9279|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-CAPABILITY-NEG</code> | Any document against a plugin whose manifest does not declare <code>caller_launch_plan</code> | <code>capability_unavailable</code>, <code>details.capability: \"caller_launch_plan\"</code>, before the plugin is invoked |\n9280|| <code>LAUNCH-PLAN-DETERMINISM-NEG</code> | Plugin returns at step 4 an argv different from its planning-role answer | <code>provider_protocol_error</code>; no process |\n9281|\n9282|Each negative case is proven by a test that fails when the gate admits the\n9283|input, driven through the real <code>ax start --launch-plan</code> entry point;\n9284|a delete-only mutant is insufficient (Appendix D.1), and the profile-flag case\n9285|MUST also survive a narrowing mutant that drops one documented alias.\n9286|\n9287|The first-checkpoint operation ID keys the capture/export and checkpoint-\n9288|publication transaction even when a backend-only provider emits a zero-entry\n9289|manifest. An identical retry reuses the same immutable objects and event;\n9290|changing either operation ID after <code>session.created</code> is\n9291|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
