{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8a9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":687,"recorded_at":1780531400001369,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1ec-8466-7681-989e-b1a3c637ad98"},"task_id":"01a0b1ec-8466-7681-989e-b1a3c637ad98","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1ec-8466-7681-989e-b1a3c637ad98","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/kkh1an-ref/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1geqhj results — ax pane enforcement wrapper\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (producer handoff; candidate UNCOMMITTED in the\n4|Story worktree on `task-board/story/STORY-260830-ptxkqe`).\n5|\n6|## Deliverable\n7|\n8|`internal/axpane`: the validation core of the `ax pane SESSION_ID`\n9|enforcement wrapper. The pure core `Decide` returns exactly one of\n10|`launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked(reason)|refused(class)`;\n11|`Run` orchestrates the adapters over the real durable stores and applies\n12|exactly the authorized effect; the bootstrap `(session_id,\n13|bootstrap_operation_id)` store binds the one recorded wrapper/child under\n14|the no-replace + fsync discipline with crash hooks; §5.2 events author\n15|through `sessrepo.AppendEvent` under the current lease; the §7.A descriptor\n16|builder supplies the provider binding context.\n17|\n18|Every check composes a landed gate (`fencing`, `matjournal`,\n19|`sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, `sessprofile`, `provhost`, `resumesmoke`,\n20|`terminalbackend`, `config`, `axerror`); nothing is re-implemented.\n21|`internal/traceability` is untouched per the Story contract (the final leaf\n22|re-pins); clause coverage lives in `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md` and the\n23|conformance matrix.\n24|\n25|## AC coverage: 41 of 41 rows driven\n26|\n27|Every command, message, state, and refusal in the AC is driven through a\n28|production entry by a named committed test. Ratio: **41 of 41**.\n29|Production call sites per row are in the conformance matrix\n30|(`TASK-260830-1geqhj_conformance-matrix.md`) and\n31|`internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`. Headline rows:\n32|\n33|- Owner epoch / fencing: lower, losing, future, foreign, expired, malformed,\n34|  absent, ambiguous, unverified, failed-handoff, remote (attach/takeover),\n35|  mode-selected entry — via `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` /\n36|  `AuthorizeRestore`.\n37|- Materialization (required + committed) and checkpoint (required + attested\n38|  + identity) — via `Decide` + `LoadMaterialization` / `LoadCheckpoint`.\n39|- Effective profile + source, `profile_mapping_unavailable` — via `Decide` →\n40|  `sessprofile.Derive` / `provhost.ResolveMapping`.\n41|- Resume tuple, identity bind, discovery bind, smoke precondition with typed\n42|  `target_auth_missing` — via `Decide` → `provhost.*` / `resumesmoke.*`.\n43|- Backend identity (`Reconcile`), closed capabilities (`CheckOperation`),\n44|  entrypoint, descriptor (`AdmitProviderDescriptor`) — via `Decide`.\n45|- Background caller `capability_unavailable` with typed realm details;\n46|  cached sentinel/`managername` structurally unauthorizing — via `Decide`.\n47|- Bootstrap idempotency (same reattach, changed mismatch, commit race),\n48|  status-proves-absence, real-kill crash seam, no-PID receipt — via\n49|  `Store.Bind` / `Store.Status` / `Run`.\n50|- `session.parked` (all four reasons, incl. offers), v4 `terminal.created` /\n51|  `session.resumed` — via `EmitParked` / `Emit` / payload builders.\n52|- After-restore steps 1-5, arm precedence, orchestrated effects — via\n53|  `Decide` / `Run`.\n54|\n55|## Validation (this worktree, this session)\n56|\n57|- `go test ./internal/axpane -count=1` — exit 0 (full package suite).\n58|- `go test ./internal/axpane -cover -count=1` — exit 0 (see coverage log).\n59|- `go test ./... -count=1` — exit 0, 38 packages ok, no FAIL.\n60|- `go test ./... -race -count=1` — exit 1 SOLELY on\n61|  `internal/sessquery` hitting the default 10m `go test` timeout\n62|  (37/38 packages ok, including `internal/axpane` in ~8s; no DATA\n63|  RACE, no individual test failure anywhere). Reran in isolation:\n64|  `go test ./internal/sessquery/ -race -count=1 -timeout 20m` —\n65|  exit 0 in 552s. The suite is pre-existing slow under race (it\n66|  needs ~9.2 minutes); my change cannot reach it (new package,\n67|  zero importers; `sessquery` reads neither README nor LOGBOOK).\n68|  Recorded honestly as a failing-as-configured gate with the\n69|  isolation evidence attached (`sessquery-rerun.log`,\n70|  `sessquery-long.log`).\n71|- `go test ./internal/axpane/ -race -count=1` — exit 0.\n72|- `go test ./internal/axpane/ -cover -count=1` — exit 0, 81.7%.\n73|- `go test ./... -cover -count=1` — exit 0 (see cover log).\n74|- `go build`, `go vet`, `gofmt` check, `GOOS=linux`/`windows` builds,\n75|  JSON census, `git diff --check` — all exit 0.\n76|- `tracecheck` — exit 0 (no registry change, as required for a first leaf).\n77|- `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` —\n78|  exit 0.\n79|- 14/14 fuzz gates (`-fuzztime=100x`) — exit 0.\n80|- `task-board validate` — exit 0 (187 pre-existing MISSING_ACTIVITY\n81|  warnings on other items, none on this task or story).\n82|- Mutant harness: 25/25 rows match — 24 narrowing mutants KILLED plus the\n83|  applied harmless SURVIVED control (`mutants.log` with per-plant raw logs\n84|  and subprocess exits).\n85|\n86|## Crash / idempotency evidence\n87|\n88|- Real-kill test `TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates` (SIGKILL after the\n89|  no-replace commit, before directory sync): the complete binding survives\n90|  and the identical retry reattaches — no torn prefix, no second child.\n91|- Hook tests pin both boundaries (aborted stage → absence + converging\n92|  retry; post-commit hook error → commit stands + reattach).\n93|- Commit-race tests pin linearizability (same-operation loser reattaches,\n94|  changed-operation loser refuses `idempotency_mismatch`).\n95|- Parked events append through the `sessrepo` owner (linkage + round-trip\n96|  proven here; the owner's own crash evidence stays with that package).\n97|\n98|## Files (all UNCOMMITTED, candidate snapshot)\n99|\n100|- `internal/axpane/doc.go`, `decide.go`, `errors.go`, `binding.go`,\n101|  `sync.go`, `events.go`, `descriptor.go`, `gates.go`, `run.go`\n102|- `internal/axpane/fixtures_test.go`, `decide_test.go`, `binding_test.go`,\n103|  `crash_unix_test.go`, `run_test.go`, `events_test.go`,\n104|  `descriptor_test.go`, `conformance_test.go`, `mutant_harness.py`,\n105|  `TRACEABILITY.md`\n106|- `README.md` (new package section, no capability/CLI claim),\n107|  `LOGBOOK.md` (newest-first entry)\n108|\n109|## Stated bounds (no unsupported claims)\n110|\n111|No `ax` CLI, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider supervision, no\n112|mesh transport, no broker. The step-2 refresh is the caller-reported\n113|`Verified` fact; signatures are caller-supplied; backend liveness and\n114|backend operations belong to the later leaf; the host-local binding arrives\n115|from the modeled backend caller; committed-phase and step-5 park readings\n116|are stated; unknown SESSION_ID refuses `invalid_arguments` (no minted\n117|code). Full list in TRACEABILITY.md.\n118|\n119|## For the reviewer\n120|\n121|Suggested entry: `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md` (41-row matrix + 25-row\n122|mutant table + bounds), then `decide.go`, then the evidence tarball\n123|(`mutants.log`, full-suite logs, race/cover logs, fuzz logs).","final_result":true}}}
