{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000caf5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1ea-9cfc-7101-8803-4405ac4e96a0"},"sequence":981,"recorded_at":1780531400001957,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e4f9005c-1c88-4d61-aae9-39ab9037f299"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1ed-b65b-7f70-bb9d-f85081607381"},"task_id":"01a0b1ed-b65b-7f70-bb9d-f85081607381","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1ed-b65b-7f70-bb9d-f85081607381","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(12198 line(s) above)\n12199|### 14.6 CLI Result 4.0.0 TerminalBackend surfaces\n12200|\n12201|CLI Result 4.0.0 retains the exact CLI Result 3 top-level success envelope,\n12202|every v1-v3 command/result body not named below, and their top-level ID rules.\n12203|It adds the closed command tags <code>terminal.backend.list</code>,\n12204|<code>terminal.backend.show</code>, <code>terminal.backend.probe</code>, and\n12205|<code>terminal.backend.doctor</code>, and replaces only the v1\n12206|<code>start</code> and <code>resume</code> success-body variants with the v4\n12207|variants below. Failures bind Structured Error 1.3.0.\n12208|\n12209|<code>TerminalBackendSummary</code> is the closed object containing exactly:\n12210|\n12211|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n12212|| --- | --- |\n12213|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n12214|| <code>implementation_version</code> / <code>protocol_version</code> | semver&#124;null; both null exactly when no trusted compatible implementation was identified |\n12215|| <code>availability</code> | <code>available&#124;unavailable&#124;unknown&#124;ambiguous&#124;untrusted&#124;incompatible</code> |\n12216|| <code>platform_compatible</code> | boolean; false for an identified wrong-platform implementation and for unknown identity |\n12217|| <code>capabilities</code> | sorted unique TerminalBackend capability[0..16], containing only currently evidenced enabled claims |\n12218|| <code>evidence_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..256] of sanitized Manifest/Probe/Capability Evidence |\n12219|| <code>diagnostic_codes</code> | sorted unique Structured Error code[0..256] |\n12220|\n12221|Null versions, an empty capability/evidence set, or diagnostic output never\n12222|means that an unknown backend is absent or that activation may use a default.\n12223|<code>TerminalInstanceSummary</code> is the closed host-local object containing\n12224|exactly <code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n12225|<code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>,\n12226|<code>terminal_backend:TerminalBackendSummary</code>,\n12227|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n12228|<code>state:absent&#124;creating&#124;parked&#124;active&#124;quiescing&#124;stopped&#124;stale_fenced&#124;unavailable</code>, and\n12229|<code>attachable:boolean</code>. It never contains a native reference, PID,\n12230|socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential/auth state, terminal output, or live-\n12231|process details.\n12232|\n12233|| Result tag | Exact body members |\n12234|| --- | --- |\n12235|| <code>terminal_backend_list</code> | <code>backends:TerminalBackendSummary[0..256]</code> sorted by backend ID, <code>registry_read:valid</code> |\n12236|| <code>terminal_backend_show</code> | <code>backend:TerminalBackendSummary</code>, <code>manifest_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>probe_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n12237|| <code>terminal_backend_probe</code> | <code>backend:TerminalBackendSummary</code>, <code>probe_id:digest</code>, <code>probed_at:timestamp</code> |\n12238|| <code>terminal_backend_doctor</code> | <code>healthy:boolean</code>, <code>backends:TerminalBackendSummary[0..256]</code>, <code>findings:CLIFinding[0..4096]</code> |\n12239|| <code>start</code> | <code>session:SessionSummary</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>terminal_instance:TerminalInstanceSummary</code> |\n12240|| <code>resume</code> | <code>session:SessionSummary</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_instance:TerminalInstanceSummary</code> |\n12241|\n12242|The command/result mapping follows the table names exactly. The four inspection\n12243|commands are read-only: they do not activate an implementation, create an\n12244|instance, attach a client, change configuration, mutate ownership, or obtain a\n12245|credential. <code>probe</code> may refresh only derived/local evidence under\n12246|Section 4.B. Start/resume success requires an <code>active</code> or\n12247|<code>parked</code> instance whose IDs/versions/generation match the validated\n12248|binding and evidence. Restore mismatch is an Error 1.3 failure, never silent\n12249|default selection.\n12250|\n12251|Legacy CLI Result 1 projection is deterministic only when the v4 summary has\n12252|backend ID <code>ax.tmux</code> or <code>ax.conpty</code>; it emits the exact\n12253|historical <code>tmux</code> or <code>conpty</code> field and, for resume, the\n12254|host-local native reference required by the immutable v1 shape. Other IDs,\n12255|missing native projection data, or an unrepresentable state return\n12256|<code>incompatible_schema</code>. Projection never rewrites a v4 result or\n12257|invents capabilities, and lower-version clients remain read-only for an\n12258|unrepresentable backend.\n12259|\n12260|### 14.7 Session selector 1.0.0 and CLI Result 5.0.0\n12261|\n12262|This section is the v0.6.0 selector contract. It applies to the umbrella\n12263|<code>ax SELECTOR</code> and every existing managed-session NAME operand in\n12264|Section 14, including status, attach, takeover, fork, stop, resume, sync,\n12265|diff, materialize, logs --session and session set-profile. Creation NAME, destination HOST,\n12266|provider-native identifiers, Directory instance IDs/query expressions, and the\n12267|internal <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code> are not selector operands. No new\n12268|product operation or ownership authority is introduced.\n12269|\n12270|#### 14.7.1 Literal grammar and source-index resolution\n12271|\n12272|A selector is one CLI argument. Ordinary shell quoting handles spaces; the CLI\n12273|MUST NOT join multiple arguments, expand aliases as shell text, decode percent\n12274|escapes, normalize Unicode, trim, or case-fold configured host aliases. Split\n12275|at the FIRST literal <code>@</code> only. The key is either a Section 2 session\n12276|NAME or <code>id:SESSION_UUID</code>, with a canonical lowercase UUIDv7; neither\n12277|key form contains <code>@</code>. A bare UUID retains Section 2.3 name-first\n12278|precedence. <code>id:</code> explicitly bypasses names and never denotes a\n12279|provider-native ID, directory instance ID, lease ID, or UUID prefix.\n12280|\n12281|| Form | Meaning |\n12282|| --- | --- |\n12283|| <code>NAME</code> / bare UUID | Exact Section 2.3 local-name, peer-name, UUID, not-found precedence; collision refusal unchanged |\n12284|| <code>id:SESSION_UUID</code> | Durable AX session UUID in the local and allowed-peer union, independent of names |\n12285|| <code>KEY@local</code> | Only the local derived source index |\n12286|| <code>KEY@peer:ALIAS</code> | Only the configured peer source whose entire remaining suffix is the literal alias |\n12287|| <code>KEY@id:HOST_UUID</code> | Only the source whose canonical host UUID is given; local UUID selects local; otherwise exactly one allowlisted configured peer |\n12288|\n12289|Examples: <code>ax status build@local</code>,\n12290|<code>ax status build@peer:workstation</code>,\n12291|<code>ax status \"build@peer:Work Laptop\"</code>,\n12292|<code>ax status \"build@peer:Ops@east:თბილისი\"</code>, and\n12293|<code>ax status id:0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab</code>.\n12294|A percent sign in an alias is literal. <code>peer:</code> with an empty alias,\n12295|unknown source prefixes, malformed durable IDs, and an empty key are invalid\n12296|arguments. The alias obeys the existing configured name bound, 1–64 characters;\n12297|this grammar adds no alias encoding, normalization, or registration path.\n12298|\n12299|Resolution first validates configuration, including uniqueness of exact alias\n12300|and host-ID mappings. Duplicate source mappings are invalid_config, never\n12301|first-match selection. An explicit unknown alias/host is selector_source_not_found;\n12302|a known but disallowed peer is peer_not_allowlisted. A failed, partial, malformed,\n12303|or inaccessible config read is invalid_config. A remote source transport/I/O read failure is selector_source_read_failed\n12304|(exit 8); a local source/store I/O failure is the existing\n12305|local_precondition_failed (exit 3). A partial or malformed index/authority\n12306|response is integrity_failure (exit 9), not absence. A complete valid empty index\n12307|or a complete index without the selected live key returns not_found. A malformed\n12308|record or digest failure is integrity_failure. These outcomes MUST remain distinct.\n12309|An explicit source MUST NOT fall back to the local index, another peer, a cached\n12310|index from another source, or a union search, even when the same name/UUID exists\n12311|there. A peer source requires a complete read of that peer's advertised index\n12312|under the selected transport, with verified configured host identity; a local\n12313|cached observation does not prove that read succeeded.\n12314|\n12315|For a qualified NAME, select in that source only: exact live name first, then\n12316|exact UUID if the NAME is UUID-shaped. Deduplicate multiple copies of the same\n12317|session UUID only when their immutable record digest agrees. Distinct live\n12318|UUIDs with the same name or ASCII-fold-colliding names return name_ambiguous.\n12319|For bare input retain exactly Section 2.3 tiers: a local exact match wins over a\n12320|peer exact match; a peer exact match wins over UUID interpretation. Collision\n12321|checks apply within the reached tier. Unread lower tiers need not be consulted\n12322|after a unique higher-tier match. A tier that must be read but cannot be read\n12323|is a read failure, not permission to proceed to a lower tier. Tombstoned entries\n12324|are excluded only with authoritative tombstone evidence, not a failed record read.\n12325|\n12326|#### 14.7.2 Resolve once, bind facts, revalidate execution\n12327|\n12328|Resolve the key to a session UUID once per invocation/confirmed plan. Build a\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
